So you want to hardcode a text file (most probably a csv)
into a a c macro?

(I hate hard coding, but some datasets like iris can be considered already hard coded into us)

this is whar claude told me

perl -pe 'chomp; $_=$.==1?"#define MAS001 \"$_ \\\n":"$_ ".(eof?"\"":"\\\n")'
```

This will:
1. First line: prefix with `#define MAS001 "` and append ` \`
2. Middle lines: append ` \`
3. Last line: append `"`

Example input:
```
line one
line two
line three
```

Example output:
```
#define MAS001 "line one \
line two \
line three"

